[al:新概念英语（四）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Patients and Doctors]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.31]Lesson 28 | 第28课
[00:02.34]Patients and doctors | 病人与医生
[00:09.46]What are patients looking for when they visit the doctor? | 病人看医生时想得到什么？
[00:14.79]This is a sceptical age, | 这是一个怀疑一切的时代，
[00:16.94]but although our faith in many of the things in which our forefathers fervently believed has weakened, | 但是尽管我们对祖先们深信不疑的许多事物的信心已经减弱，
[00:23.70]our confidence in the curative properties of the bottle of medicine remains the same as theirs. | 我们对瓶装药品疗效的信心却仍与先人一样。
[00:30.52]This modern faith in medicines is proved by the fact | 现代人对药品的信赖由这一事实所证明：
[00:34.23]that the annual drug bill of the Health Services is mounting to astronomical figures. | 即卫生部门的年度药费开支正上升到天文数字，
[00:40.51]and shows no signs at present of ceasing to rise. | 而且目前毫无停止增长的迹象。
[00:45.25]The majority of the patients attending the medical out-patients departments of our hospitals feel that | 到我们医院门诊部看病的大多数病人觉得，
[00:51.22]they have not received adequate treatment unless they are able to carry home with them | 如果他们不能随身带回家
[00:56.22]some tangible remedy in the shape of a bottle of medicine, | 某种有形的药物——一瓶药水、
[01:00.29]a box of pills, or a small jar of ointment, | 一盒药丸或一小罐药膏，
[01:04.21]and the doctor in charge of the department is only too ready to provide them with these requirements. | 他们就没有得到充分的治疗，而负责门诊的医生也总是乐于满足他们的这些要求。
[01:10.98]There is no quicker method of disposing of patients than by giving them what they are asking for, | 没有比病人要什么就给什么更快打发他们走的方法了，
[01:17.30]and since most medical men in the Health Services are overworked | 由于卫生部门的大多数医务工作者都工作过度，
[01:21.58]and have little time for offering time-consuming and little-appreciated advice on such subjects as diet, | 没有时间就饮食等题目提供费时而又不讨人喜欢的忠告，
[01:29.10]right living, and the need for abandoning bad habits etc., | 比如正确的生活方式、戒除不良习惯的必要性等等，
[01:33.81]the bottle, the box, and the jar are almost always granted them. | 药瓶、药盒和药膏罐几乎总是有求必应。
[01:39.03]Nor is it only the ignorant and ill-educated person who has such faith in the bottle of medicine. | 而且对瓶装药品抱有这种信心的不只是无知和没受过良好教育的人。
[01:45.79]It is recounted of Thomas Carlyle that when he heard of the illness of his friend, Henry Taylor, | 据说，托马斯·卡莱尔有一次听说他的朋友亨利·泰勒病了，
[01:52.98]he went off immediately to visit him, | 便立即动身前去探望，
[01:55.99]carrying with him in his pocket what remained a bottle of medicine formerly prescribed for an indisposition of Mrs. Carlyle's. | 衣袋里带着一瓶剩下的从前为卡莱尔夫人的一次不适所开的药水。
[02:06.16]Carlyle was entirely ignorant of what the bottle in his pocket contained, | 卡莱尔完全不知道他衣袋里那瓶药里装的是什么，
[02:11.22]of the nature of the illness from which his friend was suffering, | 不知道他的朋友患的是什么病，
[02:15.02]and of what had previously been wrong with his wife, | 也不知道他的妻子以前得过什么病，
[02:18.70]but a medicine that had worked so well in one form of illness would surely be of equal benefit in another, | 但是一种对某种病如此有效的药水，对另一种病想必也同样有益，
[02:25.88]and comforted by the thought of the help he was bringing to his friend, | 一想到自己正在带给朋友的帮助，他感到欣慰，
[02:30.16]he hastened to Henry Taylor's house. | 便急忙赶往亨利·泰勒的家。
[02:33.66]History does not relate whether his friend accepted his medical help, but in all probability he did. | 史书没有记载他的朋友是否接受了他的医药帮助，但十有八九接受了。
[02:40.74]The great advantage of taking medicine is that it makes no demands on the taker | 服药的一大优点是它对服药人没有任何要求，
[02:45.65]beyond that of putting up for a moment with a disgusting taste, | 只要求他暂时忍受一下令人作呕的味道，
[02:49.86]and that is what all patients demand of their doctors--to be cured at no inconvenience to themselves. | 这正是所有病人对医生的要求——在不给自己带来任何不便的情况下把病治好。
